// Local Google Health OAuth credentials -- copy to Secrets.xcconfig (gitignored) and fill in.
// Do NOT commit Secrets.xcconfig or real client IDs / secrets.
//
// Prefer an iOS OAuth client (Authorization Code + PKCE). No client secret in the app binary.
// Bundle ID on the Google Cloud OAuth client must match exactly (com.readiness.ReadinessTracker).
//
// Optional Xcode wiring:
//   1. Copy this file to Secrets.xcconfig in the repo root.
//   2. Point the ReadinessTracker target base configuration at Secrets.xcconfig (Debug & Release),
//      or set user-defined GOOGLE_HEALTH_IOS_CLIENT_ID / GOOGLE_HEALTH_IOS_REVERSED_CLIENT_ID.
//   3. Info.plist maps $(GOOGLE_HEALTH_IOS_CLIENT_ID) and registers
//      $(GOOGLE_HEALTH_IOS_REVERSED_CLIENT_ID) as a CFBundleURLSchemes entry.
//      Legacy FITBIT_CLIENT_ID / GOOGLE_HEALTH_CLIENT_ID aliases remain for older local configs.
//   4. Clean + rebuild so Bundle.main picks up the values.
//
// Empty defaults keep CI / fresh clones building without secrets.
//
// Redirect URI (Honest #361): com.googleusercontent.apps.<CLIENT_ID_PREFIX>:/oauth2redirect
//   where CLIENT_ID_PREFIX is the iOS client id without ".apps.googleusercontent.com".
//   Example: client 123-abc.apps.googleusercontent.com
//     → scheme com.googleusercontent.apps.123-abc
//     → redirect com.googleusercontent.apps.123-abc:/oauth2redirect
//   Set GOOGLE_HEALTH_IOS_REVERSED_CLIENT_ID to that scheme (Info.plist URL type).
//   FitbitManager also derives the same redirect from GOOGLE_HEALTH_IOS_CLIENT_ID at runtime.
//   Legacy readinesstracker://oauth remains registered for deep links but is NOT used as redirect_uri
//   (Google rejects custom schemes without a period → 400 invalid_request).
// Scope (sleep-first Honest #360): https://www.googleapis.com/auth/googlehealth.sleep.readonly
// Do NOT mix legacy Google Fit fitness.* scopes (omit include_granted_scopes).
// Testing mode: refresh tokens expire after ~7 days; unverified apps capped at 100 users.

GOOGLE_HEALTH_IOS_CLIENT_ID =
GOOGLE_HEALTH_IOS_REVERSED_CLIENT_ID =

// Optional aliases (FitbitManager prefers GOOGLE_HEALTH_IOS_CLIENT_ID first).
GOOGLE_HEALTH_CLIENT_ID =
FITBIT_CLIENT_ID =
